 "situation": "Four sectors of one front, from north to south: a town, a village, hill country, and fields. The Americans hold the first three sectors, and the Russians hold the fourth. The Germans attack with 9 squads under 4 leaders, 9 support weapons, and 4 armored vehicles. The Americans hold with 6 squads under 3 leaders and 1 armored vehicle, and the Russians hold the last sector with 3 squads under 1 leader and 1 support weapon. The Germans win if they end the game in control of 2 of the 4 largest stone buildings in columns U to EE, one on each board. Otherwise the Americans and the Russians win. Each American or Russian unit that sets up in a woods hex or a building hex is hidden, and the other units set up in full view. A vehicle hides only in woods or in a wooden building. A hidden unit comes on the board when it moves, fires, or makes smoke, when an attack on its hex has an effect, when an enemy enters its hex, or when an enemy is next to it at the end of a Defensive Fire Phase or an Advance Phase. The Germans move first. 12 turns.",
 "notes": "A project scenario of the library, slot L12 (owner directive, 2026-10-16), not a printed scenario. `sl-cli library` made it from draw seed 8 and board seed 4. The rule level is 44. The defending force is 877 points and the attacking force is 1461 points on the scale of slcampaign.points, a share of 5 to 3. No part of it is card text (SR-07). Balance (gate item 4, 2026-10-18): v7 against v7 gave the German attacker 813 of 1,600 games (50.8 percent), artifact runs/20261018T143547Z-library-l12-s1-10. Gate item 3: v3, v6, and v7 played it to the end on the two sides. The card agrees with the scenario, so it went into the library with no review step (owner, 2026-10-17)."
